        bookId: 'rhythm-of-war',
        text: 'Kaladin had once trusted Zahel enough to ask his advice about letting King Elhokar be killed. After Kaladin was relieved of duty for battle shock, he sought Zahel out again. Zahel easily beat him using only his clothing, which moved and fought for him, and in talking helped Kaladin see he had to find his own path rather than live by what others wanted.',
